ideo up it's  been viewed hundreds of thousands of  times and i say it is the most grotesque  form of propaganda where a british  citizen is sat there bruised handcuffed  and being interrogated this sort of  thing shouldn't be happening in the  first place but reputable social media  companies should be having nothing to do  with it  um  talking about domestic politics uh now  earlier in the program we spoke to your  colleague the conservative mp craig  whitaker he said that he thinks boris  johnson needs to step down because if  you make the law you can't then break  the law  he's right isn't he  i take a different view to craig i mean  he's a valued friend and colleague of  mine but i do think that boris johnson  is the right person to be leading the  country i can't see  at a time when there are such big issues  like a european war like a emerging and  escalating economic crisis  that we would want to get into the  territory of a leadership election and  contemplating a changing leader that  doesn't seem to me to be in the next  i've heard this argument before that you  know we're in a time of war so we can't  change the leader i mean we aren't at  what are we obviously ukraine is at war  and but also there's president for  changing prime minister and leader even  when we are at war we changed leader  during world war one twice during world  war ii well i think there's a with  respect quite poor comparisons the times  that prime ministers have resigned in  the past have generally been because  there's been a catastrophic failure of  the government's central policy like  never changing like in the eden some  people  some people would say that there's been  a catastrophic uh failure of public  confidence in the prime minister because  as we heard from a panelist quite a lot  of them think that he's lied  well your panel was actually quite split  from the conversation i heard and that  there were certainly people on the panel  who felt that this has been a sorry  ep